member.summary:
            Re-textures one X-Plane Global Scenery tile with photo terrain:


the solid land patches are joined into one mesh and cut along the photo textures' edges;

each piece is given its texture (terrain/ROW_COL_BI16.ter) and texture coordinates;

the overlays blending one land class into the next are left out;

water and every raster stay as they are, byte for byte;

the roads, forests, buildings and other objects are left out (with their definitions and the 32-bit pools of the
            roads' points): they go to the tile's overlay (), or come from another overlay package.

            Elevations X-Plane samples from the tile's raster stay sampled, so the relief is X-Plane's own.
            With , the textures near airports are of finer zooms (see ).

            Re-textures one X-Plane Global Scenery tile with photo terrain:


the solid land patches are joined into one mesh and cut along the photo textures' edges;

